    "introduction": "Smith & Nephew develops medical technology used in orthopaedics, sports medicine and wound management. Its products include joint implants, surgical tools and technologies that help clinicians treat injuries and manage wounds. Customers include hospitals, surgeons and other healthcare providers, with revenue generated through equipment and consumable-product sales. Clinical results, ease of use and support for medical professionals are important to adoption. The business combines research, regulated manufacturing and specialist sales relationships. Procedure volumes and healthcare budgets influence demand, while product innovation and reliable supply affect competitiveness. Its portfolio includes both surgical products linked to treatment activity and recurring wound-care requirements.",
